<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: Czech central bank intervenes again to support CZK.</title>
<headline>Czech central bank intervenes again to support CZK.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Czech central bank (CNB), for the second time on Thursday, again intervened on the market to support the crown, Tomas Becvar, a dealer with the country's largest commerical bank, Komercni Banka, told Reuters.</p>
<p>Tomas Novak at bank CSOB confirmed the CNB was again on the market, adding that while the first wave of intervention was at small amounts, the CNB was now using larger amounts.</p>
<p>He did not specify what amounts the CNB was using.</p>
</text>
